 "voice": [
  {
   "id": "vo01",
   "t": 0.1,
   "dur": 4.202,
   "file": "vo/01.wav",
   "text": "How does this cell fit? Its pipe is narrower than it is."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo02",
   "t": 5.1,
   "dur": 11.215,
   "file": "vo/02.wav",
   "text": "Each one is a dented disc. It even threw out its own nucleus to make room. And you've got about twenty-five trillion of them: most of your own cells."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo03",
   "t": 17.1,
   "dur": 9.568,
   "file": "vo/03.wav",
   "text": "Follow one as the pipes split, and split again, into the tiniest ones. There's no room to pass, so they go in single file."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo04",
   "t": 27.5,
   "dur": 8.31,
   "file": "vo/04.wav",
   "text": "You'd guess it just stretches to fit. It can't. That dent gives it spare skin, so it folds up neatly like a parachute instead."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo05",
   "t": 38.7,
   "dur": 8.078,
   "file": "vo/05.wav",
   "text": "The tightest squeeze is less than half its width. And it does this its whole life, over and over, for about four months."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo06",
   "t": 50.7,
   "dur": 6.653,
   "file": "vo/06.wav",
   "text": "Sickle cells lose that dent, stiffen, and can jam where oxygen gets dropped off. That dent has a job."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo07",
   "t": 58.3,
   "dur": 4.845,
   "file": "vo/07.wav",
   "text": "Meanwhile, as you watched, your bones made over a hundred million new ones."
  },
  {
   "id": "vo08",
   "t": 63.9,
   "dur": 4.14,
   "file": "vo/08.wav",
   "text": "Next: what this cell carries. Room for about a billion passengers."
  }
 ]
}